    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d361">

                <pb facs="0409" n="309" xml:id="pg309"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/2744: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jefferson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-12-11T13:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 11,
                                1920—1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>53. Your December 9, 2 p.m.</p>
                <p>You may advise the President that the suggestion of the Department was made with
                    the understanding that any new election law which might be passed in the next
                    session of the Nicaraguan Congress would not be construed as being retroactive
                    and would necessarily apply only to future elections.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
